# Assets/cursors/blank.xcursor is a binary Xcursor image. Git's auto-detection
# would almost certainly classify it as binary on its own (it is mostly NUL
# bytes), but "almost certainly" is not a good enough guarantee for a file whose
# only job is to be byte-exact on a Pi: a single CRLF translation on checkout
# corrupts the header and the compositor silently falls back to a visible
# cursor. Say it explicitly instead.
*.xcursor binary

# Shell scripts are executed on the Pi. Committed from Windows, so pin LF
# endings - a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel fail the exec with a
# "bad interpreter" error that reads as a missing file.
*.sh text eol=lf
